WEBVTT

1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,290
You're super late, Marfil.

2
00:01:01,291 --> 00:01:03,415
You can't go a second without me, huh?

3
00:01:03,416 --> 00:01:05,625
- Right.
- You need to be more independent, Tami.

4
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,124
- How's it going?
- Terribly.

5
00:01:11,125 --> 00:01:13,374
Fonteyn is in a particularly
bad mood today.

6
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:14,750
That's new.

7
00:01:39,458 --> 00:01:40,916
I can't remember the steps.

8
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,916
What do you mean...?

9
00:02:45,416 --> 00:02:48,999
Hey, that was kind of cruel,
don't you think?

10
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,957
No. She can't treat people that way.

11
00:02:50,958 --> 00:02:53,290
- Someone needs to put her in her place.
- Girl.

12
00:02:53,291 --> 00:02:54,791
I'm not talking about Fonteyn.

13
00:04:31,166 --> 00:04:35,083
BASED ON THE BOOK BY
MERCEDES RON

14
00:04:49,750 --> 00:04:51,166
Put her in the van!

15
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:59,875
DRAWN TOGETHER

16
00:05:16,708 --> 00:05:17,791
Dad?

17
00:05:19,416 --> 00:05:20,541
Marfil.

18
00:05:22,291 --> 00:05:23,415
Dad.

19
00:05:23,416 --> 00:05:24,500
How are you?

20
00:05:26,166 --> 00:05:27,291
Fine. I don't know...

21
00:05:28,416 --> 00:05:29,666
Honey.

22
00:05:31,458 --> 00:05:33,082
You scared me to death.

23
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:34,207
What happened?

24
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:35,875
You went missing two days ago.

25
00:05:37,416 --> 00:05:39,415
And last night
someone brought you to the ER.

26
00:05:39,416 --> 00:05:41,541
- What?
- It's okay.

27
00:05:43,958 --> 00:05:44,958
Lay down.

28
00:05:46,958 --> 00:05:49,499
The police were waiting
for you to wake up.

29
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,291
This won't take long, don't worry.

30
00:05:51,875 --> 00:05:53,291
I'm Officer Rivera.

31
00:05:54,333 --> 00:05:57,375
Could you tell us what happened?
Anything you remember.

32
00:05:58,333 --> 00:05:59,375
Yes.

33
00:06:00,833 --> 00:06:02,790
Someone assaulted me from behind.

34
00:06:02,791 --> 00:06:04,624
Did you see the attacker's face?

35
00:06:04,625 --> 00:06:06,750
No. No, I just...

36
00:06:07,416 --> 00:06:09,915
I just remember a voice saying,

37
00:06:09,916 --> 00:06:11,541
"Put her in the van."

38
00:06:13,625 --> 00:06:18,124
Mr. Cortés, did someone contact you
to ask for some kind of ransom?

39
00:06:18,125 --> 00:06:19,124
No.

40
00:06:19,125 --> 00:06:21,833
Well, then this is not a kidnapping.

41
00:06:22,333 --> 00:06:23,375
It's not?

42
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:24,999
What is it, then?

43
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,082
Look, I have a son in college too.

44
00:06:27,083 --> 00:06:31,082
Sometimes kids lose control,
they drink more than they should,

45
00:06:31,083 --> 00:06:34,333
take something they shouldn't take
and they end up in a bad way.

46
00:06:38,875 --> 00:06:40,041
Logan.

47
00:06:45,291 --> 00:06:47,749
Marfil, you scared the life out of us.

48
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:49,125
How are you feeling?

49
00:06:49,625 --> 00:06:53,207
Weird. I just want to go home
and get back to normal.

50
00:06:53,208 --> 00:06:54,666
- Come on.
- Let's go.

51
00:07:16,791 --> 00:07:18,541
I changed the lock on the apartment.

52
00:07:25,583 --> 00:07:26,958
What time is the flight?

53
00:07:27,541 --> 00:07:30,958
We only have five minutes.
And you still haven't told her.

54
00:07:43,875 --> 00:07:46,916
Marfil, I need to tell you something
before I go.

55
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:49,208
You're leaving?

56
00:07:50,125 --> 00:07:52,040
You're not even staying the night?

57
00:07:52,041 --> 00:07:52,875
Listen to me.

58
00:07:54,375 --> 00:07:56,916
I would never leave you alone
after what happened.

59
00:07:58,125 --> 00:07:59,750
So you'll have a bodyguard.

60
00:08:00,625 --> 00:08:02,915
No. No, no way.

61
00:08:02,916 --> 00:08:04,457
No. Dad, no.

62
00:08:04,458 --> 00:08:07,415
You don't realize how serious this is.

63
00:08:07,416 --> 00:08:10,957
It was just a warning.
They wanted to make something clear.

64
00:08:10,958 --> 00:08:11,874
What?

65
00:08:11,875 --> 00:08:13,957
That they can get to you
whenever they want.

66
00:08:13,958 --> 00:08:15,290
Who? Who's "they"?

67
00:08:15,291 --> 00:08:16,374
We don't know yet.

68
00:08:16,375 --> 00:08:17,915
And until we figure it out,

69
00:08:17,916 --> 00:08:20,540
I need to know that there is someone
always with you.

70
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:22,707
I'm old enough to take care of myself.

71
00:08:22,708 --> 00:08:23,791
This is non-negotiable.

72
00:08:24,375 --> 00:08:27,165
I don't like bodyguards!
I don't like them!

73
00:08:27,166 --> 00:08:28,499
I'm sorry, Logan. I don't.

74
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:31,290
They remind me that something bad
can happen. I don't want that!

75
00:08:31,291 --> 00:08:33,458
I don't want a repeat
of the Central Park thing.

76
00:08:34,791 --> 00:08:35,708
Marfil.

77
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:40,458
Something bad has happened.
Until we figure out how to deal with it...

78
00:08:41,416 --> 00:08:42,916
It'll only be temporary.

79
00:08:47,583 --> 00:08:49,083
Until we find out...

80
00:08:51,708 --> 00:08:53,000
Marfil.

81
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:55,750
Marfil.

82
00:09:00,750 --> 00:09:01,750
Marfil.

83
00:09:04,583 --> 00:09:05,833
He will be your bodyguard.

84
00:09:07,291 --> 00:09:08,541
Sebastian Moore.

85
00:09:10,458 --> 00:09:11,375
Pleased to meet you.

86
00:09:15,750 --> 00:09:16,583
Marfil.

87
00:09:22,583 --> 00:09:23,583
Forgive my daughter.

88
00:09:24,166 --> 00:09:26,000
She has her mother's temper.

89
00:09:27,125 --> 00:09:30,083
- That's all right.
- Sebastian will take care of your safety.

90
00:09:32,250 --> 00:09:33,957
I am asking you, please.

91
00:09:33,958 --> 00:09:36,332
I want your coexistence to be peaceful.

92
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:37,665
He's going to live with me?

93
00:09:37,666 --> 00:09:40,332
His job is to protect you 24/7.

94
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:42,624
What about college?
Will he come with me too?

95
00:09:42,625 --> 00:09:44,499
I requested that your lessons be online.

96
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,750
You're asking me to change my whole life.

97
00:09:47,708 --> 00:09:48,791
I can't believe this.

98
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,083
- This is the best option.
- For whom?

99
00:10:00,708 --> 00:10:02,082
- Marfil.
- Is this really necessary?

100
00:10:02,083 --> 00:10:03,958
I'm entrusting you
with my daughter's life.

101
00:10:05,041 --> 00:10:06,333
Don't let me down.

102
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,790
Nothing will happen to her.

103
00:10:08,791 --> 00:10:10,208
It will only be for a while.

104
00:10:11,666 --> 00:10:12,708
Logan.

105
00:10:13,375 --> 00:10:14,666
You're in good hands.

106
00:10:17,125 --> 00:10:18,333
Try to get some sleep.

107
00:10:26,666 --> 00:10:29,957
May I know exactly what orders
my father gave you?

108
00:10:29,958 --> 00:10:31,374
"Orders"?

109
00:10:31,375 --> 00:10:35,624
My duty is to protect you
and to keep Mr. Cortés informed.

110
00:10:35,625 --> 00:10:37,833
I have to put up with you in my own home.

111
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:45,207
Your father hired me to protect you,
not to listen to your complaints.

112
00:10:45,208 --> 00:10:46,125
No.

113
00:10:46,666 --> 00:10:49,207
He put a watchdog on me
because he doesn't give a shit

114
00:10:49,208 --> 00:10:51,874
who looks after me
as long as he doesn't have to.

115
00:10:51,875 --> 00:10:52,916
Okay.

116
00:10:53,833 --> 00:10:55,457
I guarantee that you won't notice...

117
00:10:55,458 --> 00:10:57,583
I guarantee that I am noticing.

118
00:10:58,791 --> 00:10:59,666
Miss.

119
00:11:00,541 --> 00:11:01,499
Miss.

120
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,457
Are you going to escort me to my bedroom?

121
00:11:03,458 --> 00:11:05,707
I understand
you don't like this situation.

122
00:11:05,708 --> 00:11:07,165
But it is what it is.

123
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,708
So it'd be best if you got used
to being with me.

124
00:11:11,083 --> 00:11:14,000
It's you who will have to get used
to being with me.

125
00:12:10,041 --> 00:12:11,333
Do you never sleep?

126
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,333
I was about to.

127
00:12:18,666 --> 00:12:20,125
How about a smile?

128
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:24,041
This guy's so rude.

129
00:12:38,250 --> 00:12:39,166
Marfil.

130
00:12:41,208 --> 00:12:45,041
If we're going to live together,
we should set some rules for...

131
00:12:46,166 --> 00:12:47,375
coexistence.

132
00:12:49,916 --> 00:12:51,333
Because of the towel?

133
00:12:51,833 --> 00:12:54,290
Force of habit.
I was living alone one day ago.

134
00:12:54,291 --> 00:12:55,915
Well, you don't anymore.

135
00:12:55,916 --> 00:12:58,000
How would you feel
if I walked around like that?

136
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,291
Try it one day, we'll see what happens.

137
00:13:21,291 --> 00:13:24,500
GABRIELA - MISSED CALL

138
00:13:29,541 --> 00:13:30,541
Crap.

139
00:13:37,666 --> 00:13:39,458
I need your help.

140
00:13:40,041 --> 00:13:41,207
What is it?

141
00:13:41,208 --> 00:13:43,374
My younger sister,

142
00:13:43,375 --> 00:13:45,999
Gabriela, lives in London.

143
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,458
But I haven't told her
about the kidnapping yet and...

144
00:13:50,291 --> 00:13:52,249
I'm worried something might happen to her.

145
00:13:52,250 --> 00:13:54,290
She's in a boarding school.
She can't get out.

146
00:13:54,291 --> 00:13:57,082
But what if Gabriela gets out and...

147
00:13:57,083 --> 00:13:59,415
I can provide security for your sister.

148
00:13:59,416 --> 00:14:03,250
In fact, I have a colleague in London.

149
00:14:04,625 --> 00:14:06,375
I can call him and ask him.

150
00:14:09,375 --> 00:14:11,541
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

151
00:14:19,291 --> 00:14:22,040
- Ray, did you hear that?
<i>- Loud and clear, buddy.</i>

152
00:14:22,041 --> 00:14:23,999
I need you to contact Wilson.

153
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,332
Wilson? Your friend? The Marine?

154
00:14:27,333 --> 00:14:30,374
<i>Tell him I need his help. He'll agree.</i>

155
00:14:30,375 --> 00:14:33,874
So, you're granting the girl
that concession.

156
00:14:33,875 --> 00:14:36,707
<i>I don't think there's any harm
in granting her one thing.</i>

157
00:14:36,708 --> 00:14:40,583
Hey, the chick at the door,
is she another concession?

158
00:14:54,750 --> 00:14:56,583
- What are you doing? Hey!
- What's going on?

159
00:14:57,916 --> 00:14:59,707
- What's she doing here?
- She's a friend.

160
00:14:59,708 --> 00:15:01,249
I can't go outside, so--

161
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:03,832
No one can come without asking me.
It could be dangerous.

162
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:06,540
What's dangerous is me being
in here with you all day.

163
00:15:06,541 --> 00:15:09,375
I swear I'll go crazy
and I'll drive you crazy too.

164
00:15:13,375 --> 00:15:15,374
Sweetie!

165
00:15:15,375 --> 00:15:18,707
- I missed you, bitch.
- Me too! I mean, seriously--

166
00:15:18,708 --> 00:15:19,665
Oh, shit.

167
00:15:19,666 --> 00:15:21,250
Sebastian, my bodyguard.

168
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,832
- Bodyguard?
- I'll explain later.

169
00:15:23,833 --> 00:15:25,124
Miss, I am going to need--

170
00:15:25,125 --> 00:15:26,957
An ID, sure.

171
00:15:26,958 --> 00:15:28,540
I know the protocol.

172
00:15:28,541 --> 00:15:29,999
My dad, you know.

173
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,625
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

174
00:15:32,666 --> 00:15:35,457
"Salazar"? Is your father
the Mexican diplomat?

175
00:15:35,458 --> 00:15:37,665
That's right.
Do you need to search my bag?

176
00:15:37,666 --> 00:15:39,582
- That won't be necessary.
- Enough formalities.

177
00:15:39,583 --> 00:15:41,415
This is weird enough as it is.

178
00:15:41,416 --> 00:15:43,457
- It's nice to meet you.
- Likewise.

179
00:15:43,458 --> 00:15:45,500
If you need me, I'll be in my room.

180
00:15:47,791 --> 00:15:49,125
Is he living with you?

181
00:15:53,416 --> 00:15:55,791
It's my best friend. He's not a threat.

182
00:15:59,083 --> 00:16:01,999
- What's up, beautiful?
- Honey!

183
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,499
- Long time no see.
- I missed you.

184
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,624
- Me too.
- Look... What's up?

185
00:16:06,625 --> 00:16:08,333
We're gonna get wasted!

186
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:14,000
And who are you?

187
00:16:15,625 --> 00:16:18,832
Wait, so Sebastian
is going to live with you

188
00:16:18,833 --> 00:16:20,832
until they catch whoever kidnapped you?

189
00:16:20,833 --> 00:16:21,833
Yeah.

190
00:16:23,166 --> 00:16:25,250
But it's really weird.
Something doesn't add up.

191
00:16:25,916 --> 00:16:29,457
Why kidnap me for a day and then
release me without asking for ransom?

192
00:16:29,458 --> 00:16:32,000
Just let it go. Look on the bright side.

193
00:16:33,041 --> 00:16:34,624
Now you don't have to go to class.

194
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:39,499
<i>Look, what happened sucks,
but at least you got something in return.</i>

195
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:41,040
<i>Can we not joke about this?</i>

196
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:43,749
- What happened is very serious.
- I wasn't joking.

197
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:44,750
"In return," huh?

198
00:16:46,583 --> 00:16:48,416
Something must've been given in return.

199
00:16:48,958 --> 00:16:51,915
My dad may not have paid the ransom,
but he must've done something.

200
00:16:51,916 --> 00:16:55,500
It doesn't matter. What matters is
that nothing happened to you.

201
00:16:57,416 --> 00:16:58,250
Come.

202
00:16:59,833 --> 00:17:01,458
Sometimes I remember things.

203
00:17:14,875 --> 00:17:18,000
I was in a dark, cold place.

204
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:21,458
<i>And there was a narrow mattress.</i>

205
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:25,250
<i>I felt tired and couldn't see well.</i>

206
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,833
<i>But I could feel someone watching me.</i>

207
00:17:32,250 --> 00:17:33,333
Have you told Sebastian?

208
00:17:33,958 --> 00:17:36,165
No. I don't trust him.

209
00:17:36,166 --> 00:17:39,499
<i>He works for my dad. If he's hiding
something from me, so is Sebastian.</i>

210
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,790
<i>Shouldn't we stay the night?</i>

211
00:17:41,791 --> 00:17:44,333
<i>- I don't want to leave you with him.
- No, that's okay.</i>

212
00:17:44,833 --> 00:17:48,499
- Do you need a ride?
- Since when are you so kind, Liam?

213
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:53,000
With all this kidnapping stuff,
I'm feeling pretty scared.

214
00:17:53,875 --> 00:17:55,708
That way I won't have to pay for a taxi.

215
00:17:57,375 --> 00:17:59,458
If you need anything, just call me, okay?

216
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:01,957
I love you, sweetie.

217
00:18:01,958 --> 00:18:02,958
<i>I love you too.</i>

218
00:18:07,666 --> 00:18:09,125
<i>Did you hear that, buddy?</i>

219
00:18:32,583 --> 00:18:35,124
- Did you make sure she's asleep?
- Yes, Ray.

220
00:18:35,125 --> 00:18:36,958
- Are you sure she's asleep?
- Yes, Ray.

221
00:18:37,541 --> 00:18:38,833
Did you check for light?

222
00:18:45,583 --> 00:18:47,333
You're a funny guy, aren't you, asshole?

223
00:18:50,125 --> 00:18:52,499
I told you we should've put cameras
in her bedroom.

224
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,083
We are not voyeurs.

225
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,749
I don't like this shit.

226
00:18:58,750 --> 00:19:00,083
So what do I do?

227
00:19:00,541 --> 00:19:02,915
Earn her trust, buddy.

228
00:19:02,916 --> 00:19:05,082
What I'm asking you to do
isn't that difficult.

229
00:19:05,083 --> 00:19:07,749
Okay, then you go. I'll stay here.

230
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:09,875
Start by being a little less rude

231
00:19:10,375 --> 00:19:12,040
and a little nicer.

232
00:19:12,041 --> 00:19:13,041
Smile.

233
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:32,250
What's this?

234
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:39,041
I got up early and made you breakfast.

235
00:19:39,708 --> 00:19:41,583
- Why?
- Why not?

236
00:19:42,375 --> 00:19:43,625
You're acting weird.

237
00:19:44,375 --> 00:19:47,582
Me? I'm just trying to be nice.

238
00:19:47,583 --> 00:19:49,166
That must be it.

239
00:19:51,208 --> 00:19:53,749
So, are you going to eat or...

240
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:55,915
No. I want to go for a run
before my lessons.

241
00:19:55,916 --> 00:19:57,166
I assume you're coming too.

242
00:20:01,583 --> 00:20:02,583
I'll get changed.

243
00:20:32,375 --> 00:20:33,957
What are you doing? Let's go.

244
00:20:33,958 --> 00:20:35,041
I need some water.

245
00:20:36,916 --> 00:20:38,333
You should change your routine.

246
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:42,916
It can be dangerous
to always do the same things.

247
00:20:44,541 --> 00:20:47,875
You always come here, right?
After your ballet class.

248
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:51,999
Have you told my dad?

249
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,000
No.

250
00:20:53,625 --> 00:20:54,875
Why do you hide it from him?

251
00:21:03,708 --> 00:21:05,625
My mother was a ballerina.

252
00:21:07,291 --> 00:21:10,540
When she died,
my dad no longer approved of my dancing.

253
00:21:10,541 --> 00:21:13,708
He didn't want to drive me to class
or come to my recitals.

254
00:21:14,750 --> 00:21:18,041
So, he decided to end it for good
and sent me to boarding school.

255
00:21:19,208 --> 00:21:20,208
I'm sorry.

256
00:21:24,916 --> 00:21:26,208
You should talk to him.

257
00:21:30,458 --> 00:21:31,750
It wouldn't do any good.

258
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,750
Besides, you don't know my dad.

259
00:21:42,291 --> 00:21:44,124
I need you to contact the Russians.

260
00:21:44,125 --> 00:21:45,958
Tell them I want to meet with Kozel.

261
00:21:47,083 --> 00:21:49,999
Alejandro, I understand you're afraid.
I am too.

262
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,290
I have no other choice.

263
00:21:51,291 --> 00:21:54,790
- She was kidnapped because of what I did.
- There were bound to be consequences.

264
00:21:54,791 --> 00:21:57,791
- You put a bomb on his plane.
- It was the perfect opportunity, Logan.

265
00:21:58,333 --> 00:22:02,458
I followed the Russians for months
and I knew all their travel plans.

266
00:22:03,166 --> 00:22:05,083
He was supposed to be on that plane.

267
00:22:05,875 --> 00:22:07,874
With Kozel, nothing is certain.

268
00:22:07,875 --> 00:22:09,415
No one has ever seen him.

269
00:22:09,416 --> 00:22:11,832
His men would rather die than betray him.

270
00:22:11,833 --> 00:22:13,416
Only one thing is certain about him.

271
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:15,000
That he is dangerous.

272
00:22:16,166 --> 00:22:17,791
And you know that better than anyone.

273
00:22:19,250 --> 00:22:20,500
I didn't start this war.

274
00:22:24,458 --> 00:22:27,624
UNITED KINGDOM

275
00:22:27,625 --> 00:22:28,957
<i>When did Dad tell you?</i>

276
00:22:28,958 --> 00:22:31,624
Yesterday, but I'd rather
you'd told me yourself.

277
00:22:31,625 --> 00:22:33,165
<i>I know, I'm sorry.</i>

278
00:22:33,166 --> 00:22:35,249
<i>I didn't want to worry you. I'm fine.</i>

279
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:37,708
- <i>And I have a bodyguard now, so...</i>
- Yeah, I know.

280
00:22:39,625 --> 00:22:40,707
Is he hot?

281
00:22:40,708 --> 00:22:42,540
Fuck off, Gabriela.

282
00:22:42,541 --> 00:22:45,457
<i>I'm just curious.
I wanna know if he's hotter than mine.</i>

283
00:22:45,458 --> 00:22:46,832
You're a doofus.

284
00:22:46,833 --> 00:22:49,624
<i>How are things going with him?
Don't give him too much trouble.</i>

285
00:22:49,625 --> 00:22:51,999
No way. He has enough trouble
with my schoolmates.

286
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:55,582
Who would think of sending a bodyguard
to a girls' boarding school?

287
00:22:55,583 --> 00:22:56,583
I know.

288
00:22:57,083 --> 00:22:58,958
<i>How are you getting along with yours?</i>

289
00:22:59,916 --> 00:23:03,250
He was kind of rude at first,
but he's been nicer lately.

290
00:23:04,333 --> 00:23:06,332
I'm getting used to having him here.

291
00:23:06,333 --> 00:23:08,540
Have you made his life miserable already?

292
00:23:08,541 --> 00:23:09,958
Just enough.

293
00:23:11,666 --> 00:23:12,666
<i>What's that?</i>

294
00:23:13,250 --> 00:23:14,416
I don't know. I'll go see.

295
00:23:15,208 --> 00:23:17,249
I'll talk to you soon. Bye.

296
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:18,582
<i>Wait, Marfil.</i>

297
00:23:18,583 --> 00:23:20,833
<i>I need to ask you
a very important question.</i>

298
00:23:22,208 --> 00:23:23,291
He's very hot, isn't he?

299
00:23:24,583 --> 00:23:25,790
A little, okay?

300
00:23:25,791 --> 00:23:27,582
I knew it.

301
00:23:27,583 --> 00:23:28,750
<i>All right.</i>

302
00:23:44,125 --> 00:23:46,250
Did you hang a punching bag
without asking me?

303
00:23:48,625 --> 00:23:49,625
I'm sorry.

304
00:23:50,875 --> 00:23:51,875
I can take it down.

305
00:23:52,625 --> 00:23:54,415
- No. That's okay.
- Thanks.

306
00:23:54,416 --> 00:23:56,541
It's hard for me to be
cooped up in here all day.

307
00:23:57,500 --> 00:23:58,583
I need

308
00:23:59,875 --> 00:24:01,291
to let off steam sometimes.

309
00:24:01,833 --> 00:24:02,666
Really?

310
00:24:03,583 --> 00:24:05,041
I'm talking about working out.

311
00:24:06,958 --> 00:24:11,083
So tell me, besides boxing,

312
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,833
is there any other way you let off steam?

313
00:24:14,666 --> 00:24:16,208
I know other techniques.

314
00:24:16,875 --> 00:24:18,000
Can you teach me some?

315
00:24:18,875 --> 00:24:21,083
I don't think that's a good idea.

316
00:24:23,208 --> 00:24:24,624
Why not?

317
00:24:24,625 --> 00:24:26,125
It would be a waste of time.

318
00:24:26,791 --> 00:24:28,250
"A waste of time"?

319
00:24:31,083 --> 00:24:32,083
Are you scared?

320
00:24:33,750 --> 00:24:34,833
Are you scared of me?

321
00:24:35,958 --> 00:24:36,833
Of you?

322
00:24:37,875 --> 00:24:38,875
Tell me.

323
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:40,915
Don't touch me.

324
00:24:40,916 --> 00:24:42,749
- Are you scared...
- Enough.

325
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:45,957
- ...I'll beat the hell out of you, soldier?
- Enough, Marfil. Stop.

326
00:24:45,958 --> 00:24:46,958
Answer me.

327
00:24:47,583 --> 00:24:51,333
What lethal technique are you going to use
to defend yourself against me?

328
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,290
- Answer me.
- That's enough.

329
00:24:54,291 --> 00:24:55,582
Do you want me to stop?

330
00:24:55,583 --> 00:24:56,750
Well, then--

331
00:25:12,250 --> 00:25:13,333
Can you do that again?

332
00:25:17,125 --> 00:25:18,333
And I'll leave you alone.

333
00:25:45,500 --> 00:25:46,500
Now you.

334
00:26:23,083 --> 00:26:25,000
Were you expecting me?

335
00:26:26,208 --> 00:26:27,041
Your heels.

336
00:26:29,208 --> 00:26:30,041
Good hearing.

337
00:26:31,041 --> 00:26:34,207
I just remembered I have to go to a party.

338
00:26:34,208 --> 00:26:36,707
- I guess you're coming.
- Doesn't sound like a good idea.

339
00:26:36,708 --> 00:26:39,290
Okay. I'll call
and say we're having it here.

340
00:26:39,291 --> 00:26:40,625
Maybe I won't let them in.

341
00:26:41,208 --> 00:26:42,833
- Good luck with that.
- Okay.

342
00:26:46,333 --> 00:26:47,957
Sebastian, come on.

343
00:26:47,958 --> 00:26:49,250
Just for a little while.

344
00:26:49,875 --> 00:26:52,083
I need to go out and unwind.

345
00:26:54,541 --> 00:26:55,500
Please?

346
00:26:56,916 --> 00:26:59,375
Okay. But only for a couple of hours.

347
00:27:00,666 --> 00:27:02,083
How soon can you be ready?

348
00:27:03,583 --> 00:27:05,625
- I'll wait in the living room.
- And one thing.

349
00:27:06,625 --> 00:27:08,125
I hope it's a quiet party.

350
00:27:19,166 --> 00:27:20,333
You're staying with me.

351
00:27:22,166 --> 00:27:23,166
Marfil.

352
00:27:37,583 --> 00:27:39,416
Can you leave my coat there, please?

353
00:27:40,250 --> 00:27:42,416
Grab me a beer. I'll wait here.

354
00:27:51,125 --> 00:27:52,374
Peekaboo!

355
00:27:52,375 --> 00:27:54,458
- What's up?
- Girl!

356
00:27:57,333 --> 00:27:59,665
You brought Mr. Smiles-A-Lot, huh?

357
00:27:59,666 --> 00:28:02,457
Dude, poor guy. Look at him.
Don't you feel sorry for him?

358
00:28:02,458 --> 00:28:04,832
No. He's having a great time.

359
00:28:04,833 --> 00:28:07,040
Right. Not as much as you teasing him.

360
00:28:07,041 --> 00:28:09,374
You know what they say
about people who quarrel.

361
00:28:09,375 --> 00:28:11,624
They end up hooking up.

362
00:28:11,625 --> 00:28:12,833
Like you two?

363
00:28:14,708 --> 00:28:17,708
You don't offer a ride to a girl
if you're not interested in her.

364
00:28:18,250 --> 00:28:20,625
And I've never seen you
accept a ride from anyone.

365
00:28:22,375 --> 00:28:23,540
- Yeah, you do that.
- Yes.

366
00:28:23,541 --> 00:28:24,958
What do you mean, a drink? Liam.

367
00:28:26,708 --> 00:28:29,541
You don't see him as a playboy
and a party boy anymore?

368
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:33,249
Yes, I still think
he's a playboy and a party boy,

369
00:28:33,250 --> 00:28:37,290
but, before I realized it,
we clicked and we started dating--

370
00:28:37,291 --> 00:28:38,500
You like him a lot.

371
00:28:39,125 --> 00:28:40,665
- No.
- You like him a lot.

372
00:28:40,666 --> 00:28:42,666
- I don't like him a lot.
- That's crazy.

373
00:28:45,375 --> 00:28:46,875
You goofball.

374
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:49,375
You're so silly.

375
00:29:16,583 --> 00:29:18,374
Hey, did you say hi to Lisa?

376
00:29:18,375 --> 00:29:20,332
- What?
- Did you say hi to Lisa?

377
00:29:20,333 --> 00:29:21,915
No. Where is she?

378
00:29:21,916 --> 00:29:24,665
She was giving shots
to everyone over there.

379
00:29:24,666 --> 00:29:26,040
Dude, she's hammered.

380
00:29:26,041 --> 00:29:27,250
Let's go get her.

381
00:29:39,916 --> 00:29:41,541
Fucking pig.

382
00:30:32,583 --> 00:30:35,166
- Okay, but what about Liam?
- Wait for me here.

383
00:30:39,708 --> 00:30:41,500
What are you going to do? Sebastian!

384
00:30:50,791 --> 00:30:52,832
I'd rather you yell at me
than not talk to me.

385
00:30:52,833 --> 00:30:55,374
I'm not going to yell at you
for helping your friend.

386
00:30:55,375 --> 00:30:57,874
But in the future,
you should use a hold on someone

387
00:30:57,875 --> 00:31:00,249
only to get out of trouble,
not to get into trouble.

388
00:31:00,250 --> 00:31:03,666
- I didn't know he'd react that way.
- What did you expect?

389
00:31:04,458 --> 00:31:05,625
If I hadn't been there...

390
00:31:06,125 --> 00:31:09,666
That guy was twice your size.
You can't beat him.

391
00:31:10,291 --> 00:31:12,125
You lack the strength and the technique.

392
00:31:12,833 --> 00:31:14,082
What if I had it?

393
00:31:14,083 --> 00:31:16,249
It's not that easy. It's not magic.

394
00:31:16,250 --> 00:31:17,749
So, why don't you teach me more?

395
00:31:17,750 --> 00:31:21,250
Marfil, I taught you one chokehold,
and you saw what happened.

396
00:31:22,375 --> 00:31:24,750
If I'd known how to fight,
I could've helped.

397
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:30,958
Go ahead, laugh. But how did I do?

398
00:31:36,041 --> 00:31:37,250
You never give up, do you?

399
00:31:38,375 --> 00:31:39,666
You're getting to know me.

400
00:31:40,208 --> 00:31:42,708
Honestly, you were very quick.

401
00:31:43,583 --> 00:31:45,875
And you executed it just as I taught you.

402
00:31:46,541 --> 00:31:47,790
I have a good memory.

403
00:31:47,791 --> 00:31:48,791
Just like elephants.

404
00:31:50,791 --> 00:31:51,791
Okay.

405
00:31:52,750 --> 00:31:54,583
If I train you,
I want something in return.

406
00:31:55,500 --> 00:31:56,790
- I can pay you.
- No.

407
00:31:56,791 --> 00:31:58,583
I want three hours to myself.

408
00:31:59,291 --> 00:32:00,500
Out of this apartment.

409
00:32:01,250 --> 00:32:03,041
While you stay here.

410
00:32:04,208 --> 00:32:05,791
Don't you prefer money?

411
00:32:07,791 --> 00:32:10,375
Okay. Three hours. All right.

412
00:32:11,333 --> 00:32:13,000
We start at 6:00. Tomorrow.

413
00:32:14,041 --> 00:32:15,041
Great.

414
00:32:15,541 --> 00:32:16,541
In the morning.

415
00:32:32,833 --> 00:32:34,333
One minute.

416
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:38,582
Besides ballet,
have you practiced any other sports?

417
00:32:38,583 --> 00:32:40,041
I can ride a horse.

418
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,458
Contact sports?

419
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,707
Define "contact."

420
00:32:45,708 --> 00:32:46,833
Focus.

421
00:32:49,625 --> 00:32:52,165
You're not making it easy.

422
00:32:52,166 --> 00:32:53,082
What?

423
00:32:53,083 --> 00:32:56,791
Nothing. I said I hope it's easy,
because I'm still half asleep.

424
00:33:02,291 --> 00:33:03,874
Since you're so cocky,

425
00:33:03,875 --> 00:33:07,416
you're bound to face hand-to-hand combat
at some point, like yesterday.

426
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:09,624
I'll teach you a couple of tricks.

427
00:33:09,625 --> 00:33:11,250
Tricks for hand-to-hand combat?

428
00:33:11,791 --> 00:33:13,875
I know a few tricks too.

429
00:33:14,958 --> 00:33:15,957
You speak Russian?

430
00:33:15,958 --> 00:33:17,458
Of course. My mom was Russian.

431
00:33:19,625 --> 00:33:20,541
Okay.

432
00:33:21,041 --> 00:33:22,582
Since you're small and thin,

433
00:33:22,583 --> 00:33:25,040
your punches need to be very precise

434
00:33:25,041 --> 00:33:28,374
and land in very specific spots
to knock out your opponent ASAP.

435
00:33:28,375 --> 00:33:30,082
Hit and run, like a coward.

436
00:33:30,083 --> 00:33:32,249
No, like a sensible person.

437
00:33:32,250 --> 00:33:36,041
Remember, the key spots are here,
here, here...

438
00:33:37,250 --> 00:33:39,125
and, well, here.

439
00:33:40,375 --> 00:33:42,458
How you strike is very important.

440
00:33:43,166 --> 00:33:45,915
A very quick punch
using all your strength.

441
00:33:45,916 --> 00:33:46,916
One.

442
00:33:49,250 --> 00:33:50,250
Two.

443
00:33:52,583 --> 00:33:56,125
Not bad, but kind of weak.

444
00:33:59,250 --> 00:34:00,833
How long have you been doing ballet?

445
00:34:01,458 --> 00:34:02,458
Since I was little.

446
00:34:04,333 --> 00:34:05,625
Can you kick here?

447
00:34:09,875 --> 00:34:11,166
Okay. How about this high?

448
00:34:16,666 --> 00:34:18,750
- You have great legs.
- Thanks.

449
00:34:19,375 --> 00:34:22,707
Okay. I'm going to teach you
a couple of self-defense techniques.

450
00:34:22,708 --> 00:34:25,666
You know, hit and run.

451
00:34:26,750 --> 00:34:28,000
What if I can't run away?

452
00:34:30,750 --> 00:34:34,458
I don't want you to teach me how to run.
I want to learn how to fight.

453
00:34:39,166 --> 00:34:40,415
Are you okay?

454
00:34:40,416 --> 00:34:41,499
Did I hurt you?

455
00:34:41,500 --> 00:34:42,541
I'm great.

456
00:34:43,041 --> 00:34:46,000
When you fall five times in a row,
you learn how to land.

457
00:34:51,166 --> 00:34:52,708
Try it. Knock me down.

458
00:35:03,541 --> 00:35:05,541
You always remember all the moves.

459
00:35:06,916 --> 00:35:08,000
Just like elephants.

460
00:35:08,875 --> 00:35:10,166
Okay, we're done, aren't we?

461
00:35:10,750 --> 00:35:12,207
Yes, of course.

462
00:35:12,208 --> 00:35:14,291
After ten more minutes
of punching the bag.

463
00:35:14,916 --> 00:35:16,082
Are you serious?

464
00:35:16,083 --> 00:35:17,375
I told you it was hard.

465
00:35:18,166 --> 00:35:19,833
But if you think you can't do it...

466
00:35:24,166 --> 00:35:25,541
"I told you it was hard."

467
00:35:33,125 --> 00:35:34,290
Good morning.

468
00:35:34,291 --> 00:35:36,000
Mr. Cortés is expecting you.

469
00:35:36,625 --> 00:35:37,625
I know.

470
00:35:43,958 --> 00:35:46,875
They agree to a meeting,
but Kozel won't be there.

471
00:35:47,958 --> 00:35:48,958
He has to be there.

472
00:35:49,916 --> 00:35:51,458
After the plane thing...

473
00:35:58,000 --> 00:35:59,000
Offer him the routes.

474
00:35:59,666 --> 00:36:02,416
- I beg your pardon?
- It's the only way to convince him.

475
00:36:03,500 --> 00:36:06,082
- To let him think I'll give them to him.
- What?

476
00:36:06,083 --> 00:36:08,875
If Kozel suspects it's a trap,
he'll kill us all.

477
00:36:11,750 --> 00:36:13,458
Don't forget your place, Logan.

478
00:36:15,750 --> 00:36:16,750
Set up that meeting.

479
00:36:17,458 --> 00:36:21,083
When they see his face, he'll be doomed.
And we'll be safe out of the country.

480
00:36:21,833 --> 00:36:24,750
And bring my daughters.
I want to tell them in person.

481
00:36:44,333 --> 00:36:46,165
I'm taking my three hours.

482
00:36:46,166 --> 00:36:48,208
Fancy a burger
from that place on the corner?

483
00:36:51,041 --> 00:36:51,916
Yeah.

484
00:36:54,333 --> 00:36:55,875
Grab a couple on your way back.

485
00:36:56,541 --> 00:36:59,083
- I'm not going that far.
- Where are you going, then?

486
00:36:59,666 --> 00:37:01,375
See you later, Elephant.

487
00:37:14,333 --> 00:37:16,207
You told me to be nicer.

488
00:37:16,208 --> 00:37:19,415
Yes, to be nicer.
Not to frolic with her on the floor.

489
00:37:19,416 --> 00:37:20,708
She asked me to train her.

490
00:37:21,333 --> 00:37:24,082
It's the best way to keep her at home
while I'm here.

491
00:37:24,083 --> 00:37:25,666
You know, she reminds me of someone.

492
00:37:26,500 --> 00:37:29,957
She's disciplined, but cheeky, stubborn...

493
00:37:29,958 --> 00:37:33,457
You know those people who don't listen?
They never listen.

494
00:37:33,458 --> 00:37:34,750
Does that ring a bell?

495
00:37:49,750 --> 00:37:52,500
Do you think she suspects anything
about her father's business?

496
00:37:53,041 --> 00:37:54,166
No, I don't think so.

497
00:37:55,541 --> 00:37:57,874
Cortés has always kept her away from him.

498
00:37:57,875 --> 00:37:59,833
No wonder,
after what they did to her mother.

499
00:38:02,208 --> 00:38:05,125
Alejandro is pushing for
a face-to-face meeting with Marcus Kozel.

500
00:38:05,708 --> 00:38:06,833
Do you think he'll agree?

501
00:38:07,333 --> 00:38:08,415
Well, I don't know.

502
00:38:08,416 --> 00:38:10,999
You know no one
has ever seen that bastard.

503
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:13,958
And if anyone saw him,
they didn't live to tell the tale.

504
00:38:18,916 --> 00:38:21,500
I gotta go. Anything else?

505
00:38:26,666 --> 00:38:28,415
Keep your distance with Marfil.

506
00:38:28,416 --> 00:38:29,500
I know how to do my job.

507
00:38:30,333 --> 00:38:31,916
Okay? I'm not a rookie.

508
00:38:32,833 --> 00:38:33,958
Who do you think I am?

509
00:38:42,541 --> 00:38:44,625
That hook... Block. There.

510
00:38:46,208 --> 00:38:47,791
That's better. Easy.

511
00:38:49,541 --> 00:38:51,041
- Hold on. Okay.
- Okay.

512
00:39:24,166 --> 00:39:25,708
LOGAN
Kozel agrees to the meeting.

513
00:40:49,625 --> 00:40:52,958
<i>Sebastian, go and take
a cold shower right now.</i>

514
00:41:03,208 --> 00:41:04,791
Right... But...

515
00:41:05,833 --> 00:41:08,083
That's not keeping your distance.

516
00:41:09,250 --> 00:41:11,165
I don't know what you think
you're seeing there, but--

517
00:41:11,166 --> 00:41:12,915
You're trying to fool me.

518
00:41:12,916 --> 00:41:14,458
Do I look like an idiot?

519
00:41:14,958 --> 00:41:17,457
No more of this training nonsense.

520
00:41:17,458 --> 00:41:19,583
You're going to get into trouble, brother.

521
00:41:21,958 --> 00:41:23,416
You like that girl.

522
00:41:24,708 --> 00:41:25,833
And she likes you.

523
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:31,290
Don't even think about it. Stop.

524
00:41:31,291 --> 00:41:34,999
In two days, they leave for Spain.
And if all goes well, this will be over.

525
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:38,749
She'll start a new life,
and you'll move on with yours. Apart.

526
00:41:38,750 --> 00:41:42,040
- Got it?
- Okay. Take it easy, man.

527
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:44,582
Just because we get along
doesn't mean anything.

528
00:41:44,583 --> 00:41:45,916
I'm not going to screw it up.

529
00:41:52,041 --> 00:41:53,583
Sebastian.

530
00:41:55,250 --> 00:41:56,500
I'll be watching you.

531
00:42:03,250 --> 00:42:04,458
What are you doing up?

532
00:42:07,375 --> 00:42:10,707
My dad wants me to fly to Spain
this weekend. Did you know something?

533
00:42:10,708 --> 00:42:12,666
Only that I have to go with you.

534
00:42:14,625 --> 00:42:16,582
- Where are you going?
- To bed.

535
00:42:16,583 --> 00:42:17,708
When you go out...

536
00:42:20,125 --> 00:42:21,791
do you go visit your family?

537
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:24,208
A friend?

538
00:42:26,625 --> 00:42:30,083
That's right, go recharge your batteries.
Tomorrow I'm going to beat you up bad.

539
00:42:35,583 --> 00:42:36,666
About that.

540
00:42:37,375 --> 00:42:38,958
There will be no more training.

541
00:42:40,708 --> 00:42:41,833
Why not?

542
00:42:43,041 --> 00:42:46,750
Because I've already
taught you everything I know.

543
00:42:47,916 --> 00:42:49,082
Yeah, right.

544
00:42:49,083 --> 00:42:52,791
Yeah, and you've learned very fast.

545
00:42:53,500 --> 00:42:54,750
I'm actually...

546
00:42:57,666 --> 00:42:58,916
very proud of you.

547
00:43:03,958 --> 00:43:04,958
Good night.

548
00:43:06,916 --> 00:43:08,875
At least give me one last lesson.

549
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:11,250
As a farewell.

550
00:43:13,166 --> 00:43:14,166
Okay.

551
00:43:15,500 --> 00:43:16,916
But it'll be the last one.

552
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:42,249
You're up early.

553
00:43:42,250 --> 00:43:43,333
I know, right?

554
00:43:44,666 --> 00:43:47,124
Is there anything
you need to go over or practice?

555
00:43:47,125 --> 00:43:48,125
Tell me what you want.

556
00:43:49,125 --> 00:43:50,500
I want your three hours.

557
00:43:52,208 --> 00:43:53,916
And I'm going to fight for them.

558
00:43:55,833 --> 00:43:57,083
One bout.

559
00:43:59,291 --> 00:44:00,499
And if I win--

560
00:44:00,500 --> 00:44:03,500
It would be a miracle
if you managed to even hit me.

561
00:44:04,125 --> 00:44:05,291
Okay.

562
00:44:06,166 --> 00:44:08,458
If I can hit you once,

563
00:44:09,666 --> 00:44:12,165
you'll spend
your three hours with me today.

564
00:44:12,166 --> 00:44:15,458
And the bodyguard stays here.
Just you and me outside this apartment.

565
00:44:17,166 --> 00:44:19,999
That's a very strange way
to ask me out on a date.

566
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:22,791
I'm not asking you out.
If I did, you'd say no.

567
00:44:24,291 --> 00:44:25,916
So, I'm going to fight for it.

568
00:44:28,416 --> 00:44:30,416
What's in it for me?

569
00:44:32,041 --> 00:44:33,583
This is getting interesting.

570
00:44:36,750 --> 00:44:37,791
What do you want?

571
00:44:42,875 --> 00:44:45,041
For you to keep your distance.

572
00:44:47,083 --> 00:44:48,375
Okay.

573
00:44:57,791 --> 00:44:59,791
Whenever you're ready, Elephant.

574
00:45:13,541 --> 00:45:14,875
Not so cocky anymore.

575
00:45:32,250 --> 00:45:34,457
I thought you were only going
to use one hand.

576
00:45:34,458 --> 00:45:36,291
Well, I've changed my mind.

577
00:45:40,583 --> 00:45:41,416
Come on.

578
00:46:04,791 --> 00:46:06,125
I won, Sebastian Moore.

579
00:46:07,375 --> 00:46:08,375
Looks like it.

580
00:46:11,250 --> 00:46:12,791
Your three hours are mine.

581
00:47:39,666 --> 00:47:41,166
How long have you been there?

582
00:47:42,166 --> 00:47:46,291
Long enough to notice that's not ballet.

583
00:47:52,875 --> 00:47:55,833
It's very rude to spy on people,
just so you know.

584
00:48:20,125 --> 00:48:23,166
- Let's go. You're in for a long night.
- Okay.

585
00:48:23,958 --> 00:48:27,665
But as soon as we set foot
in the apartment, the date's over.

586
00:48:27,666 --> 00:48:29,166
Sure. Of course.

587
00:48:44,583 --> 00:48:45,625
I'm driving.

588
00:48:47,083 --> 00:48:48,416
Don't even think about it.

589
00:48:50,083 --> 00:48:53,249
I said I wanted to go out with you,
not my bodyguard.

590
00:48:53,250 --> 00:48:54,375
Can't we just walk?

591
00:48:55,166 --> 00:48:56,790
Manhattan isn't that big.

592
00:48:56,791 --> 00:48:59,333
Who said we're staying in Manhattan?

593
00:49:27,541 --> 00:49:28,665
Why are we in Brooklyn?

594
00:49:28,666 --> 00:49:31,125
We're going to eat
the best burgers in New York.

595
00:49:32,875 --> 00:49:34,333
I'm surprised you remembered.

596
00:49:36,916 --> 00:49:38,250
An elephant never forgets.

597
00:49:39,541 --> 00:49:40,541
Never.

598
00:49:46,458 --> 00:49:48,583
How did you know
this is my favorite joint?

599
00:49:49,166 --> 00:49:51,332
I have my secrets too.

600
00:49:51,333 --> 00:49:52,333
Amazing.

601
00:49:55,208 --> 00:49:56,041
What?

602
00:49:58,041 --> 00:50:00,416
Relax. Ketchup doesn't look bad on you.

603
00:50:01,291 --> 00:50:05,458
But I thought you'd be
more into light meals than sandwiches.

604
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:08,291
There's only one sandwich I like.
Taylor Ham.

605
00:50:10,625 --> 00:50:11,916
A girl like you?

606
00:50:13,291 --> 00:50:15,125
I thought you'd pick something more...

607
00:50:16,458 --> 00:50:17,624
sophisticated.

608
00:50:17,625 --> 00:50:20,040
By "sophisticated,"
you mean "posh," I assume.

609
00:50:20,041 --> 00:50:22,958
- You assume many things.
- You have no idea.

610
00:50:26,958 --> 00:50:28,250
Okay, seriously now.

611
00:50:30,291 --> 00:50:32,125
What would you like to do with your life?

612
00:50:33,166 --> 00:50:34,333
In the future.

613
00:50:35,500 --> 00:50:37,207
Well, I study Economics

614
00:50:37,208 --> 00:50:40,833
because at some point
I will have to work in my dad's company.

615
00:50:41,625 --> 00:50:44,915
My family always had ships, planes.

616
00:50:44,916 --> 00:50:47,040
Later, they built airstrips.

617
00:50:47,041 --> 00:50:49,958
Wherever there's a transport route,
he's behind it.

618
00:50:51,750 --> 00:50:53,583
You're telling me about your father.

619
00:50:54,541 --> 00:50:55,833
But what do you want to do?

620
00:50:58,333 --> 00:50:59,833
What do you really want to do?

621
00:51:05,000 --> 00:51:06,000
I just...

622
00:51:06,500 --> 00:51:07,500
I don't know.

623
00:51:12,250 --> 00:51:14,208
I just know that I want a different life.

624
00:51:16,541 --> 00:51:20,541
But I feel like my dad's always been
setting the course of my life.

625
00:51:21,416 --> 00:51:24,083
He decides where I live,
what I study, what I have to do.

626
00:51:24,958 --> 00:51:27,250
That's why I like to keep ballet a secret.

627
00:51:30,166 --> 00:51:32,625
And I want to make my own decisions.

628
00:51:34,375 --> 00:51:35,958
And to do something worthwhile.

629
00:51:36,708 --> 00:51:38,250
Something that makes my life count.

630
00:51:46,125 --> 00:51:47,541
We have to go.

631
00:51:48,750 --> 00:51:50,374
No, we'll be late. Come on.

632
00:51:50,375 --> 00:51:52,833
- What's the rush? Where are we going?
- Dancing.

633
00:51:54,583 --> 00:51:55,790
Dancing?

634
00:51:55,791 --> 00:51:58,707
I'm kidding. I don't want to lose my toes.

635
00:51:58,708 --> 00:51:59,916
But I know how to dance.

636
00:52:00,750 --> 00:52:01,750
You?

637
00:52:07,500 --> 00:52:09,166
I wish I'd known sooner.

638
00:52:09,666 --> 00:52:10,666
All in good time.

639
00:52:16,041 --> 00:52:18,000
No. It's not possible.

640
00:52:19,375 --> 00:52:20,541
We're going to the movies?

641
00:52:21,833 --> 00:52:23,875
There's a movie I wanna watch with you.

642
00:52:28,583 --> 00:52:30,415
- I'm out of here.
- Yeah, right. No way.

643
00:52:30,416 --> 00:52:32,374
Come here.

644
00:52:32,375 --> 00:52:34,374
Really? Is there nothing else on?

645
00:52:34,375 --> 00:52:36,583
<i>An Officer and a Gentleman,</i>
but I prefer this.

646
00:52:43,250 --> 00:52:44,958
Guess what my favorite scene is.

647
00:52:47,500 --> 00:52:50,083
When Rachel leaves on her private plane

648
00:52:50,625 --> 00:52:53,374
and Frank, from a distance,
can only watch her take off,

649
00:52:53,375 --> 00:52:57,958
but at the last moment, she asks them
to stop the plane to get off,

650
00:52:58,791 --> 00:53:00,915
and he runs into her arms and they kiss

651
00:53:00,916 --> 00:53:03,125
as the most beautiful
love song ever plays.

652
00:53:10,708 --> 00:53:12,790
You're going to get us kicked out.

653
00:53:12,791 --> 00:53:14,540
Okay, but don't act all tough.

654
00:53:14,541 --> 00:53:15,832
- It was funny.
- No.

655
00:53:15,833 --> 00:53:17,124
What do you mean, no?

656
00:53:17,125 --> 00:53:18,083
You're laughing.

657
00:53:18,500 --> 00:53:19,749
I can see you.

658
00:53:19,750 --> 00:53:21,499
- You're laughing.
- Stop.

659
00:53:21,500 --> 00:53:23,916
- You're laughing. I see you. Don't lie.
- Stop it.

660
00:54:39,583 --> 00:54:40,458
What?

661
00:54:42,666 --> 00:54:45,208
We're not in the apartment yet.
We're still on the date.

662
00:55:16,375 --> 00:55:17,708
The date's over.

663
00:55:19,208 --> 00:55:20,375
I'm sorry.

664
00:55:22,416 --> 00:55:23,540
What's wrong?

665
00:55:23,541 --> 00:55:24,750
I can't, I'm sorry.

666
00:55:27,041 --> 00:55:28,625
Just a second ago you could.

667
00:55:30,916 --> 00:55:31,916
Look at me.

668
00:55:33,291 --> 00:55:36,207
Why are you acting like this?
What's wrong?

669
00:55:36,208 --> 00:55:37,790
I'm not acting any particular way.

670
00:55:37,791 --> 00:55:40,582
- Can we talk about what just happened?
- Nothing just happened.

671
00:55:40,583 --> 00:55:42,249
- You just kissed me.
- Enough.

672
00:55:42,250 --> 00:55:43,749
We leave early in the morning.

673
00:55:43,750 --> 00:55:46,124
I'm going to sleep. Okay? Thank you.

674
00:55:46,125 --> 00:55:48,250
Sebastian, stop. Stop, please.

675
00:55:49,958 --> 00:55:51,125
Go to your room.

676
00:55:51,791 --> 00:55:53,208
Only if you come with me.

677
00:55:56,583 --> 00:55:58,000
Why are you so afraid?

678
00:55:59,541 --> 00:56:00,541
I'm not.

679
00:56:02,083 --> 00:56:04,791
I just want you to keep your distance.
I told you.

680
00:56:09,750 --> 00:56:11,000
Okay, I'll go to my room.

681
00:56:13,375 --> 00:56:15,083
But I'm going to leave the door open.

682
00:56:16,625 --> 00:56:19,125
Either you come in or you stay out.

683
00:56:20,541 --> 00:56:21,541
Forever.

684
00:57:23,666 --> 00:57:30,000
SPAIN

685
00:57:32,791 --> 00:57:34,708
- Marfil!
- Honey!

686
00:57:36,666 --> 00:57:39,499
I missed you so much.

687
00:57:39,500 --> 00:57:42,457
- You look so beautiful!
- So do you!

688
00:57:42,458 --> 00:57:44,415
- My girl.
- How are you?

689
00:57:44,416 --> 00:57:45,790
Good. You? Exhausted.

690
00:57:45,791 --> 00:57:48,333
- Hey, is that your bodyguard?
- Yeah, that's him.

691
00:57:49,791 --> 00:57:51,582
Not bad at all.

692
00:57:51,583 --> 00:57:53,999
- What are we doing here, Dad?
- Spending time together.

693
00:57:54,000 --> 00:57:55,333
Isn't that wonderful?

694
00:57:56,833 --> 00:57:58,416
Yeah, but why?

695
00:58:01,250 --> 00:58:03,708
Because I'd like us to say goodbye

696
00:58:04,583 --> 00:58:06,625
to the house where we've been so happy.

697
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:08,791
You're selling the house?

698
00:58:09,625 --> 00:58:12,583
Girls, what do you think of Buenos Aires?

699
00:58:13,958 --> 00:58:15,665
- Buenos Aires?
- What?

700
00:58:15,666 --> 00:58:19,666
Why not? A change of scenery,
of people, of perspective.

701
00:58:21,791 --> 00:58:23,333
Is this because of the kidnapping?

702
00:58:24,625 --> 00:58:26,874
- This is because I was kidnapped.
- No.

703
00:58:26,875 --> 00:58:29,499
It's because I got a very good offer
for the company.

704
00:58:29,500 --> 00:58:30,708
You're selling the company?

705
00:58:31,083 --> 00:58:32,915
Is that what they asked in return?

706
00:58:32,916 --> 00:58:34,791
You made a deal so they would let me go.

707
00:58:36,250 --> 00:58:37,790
Is that it? Did you make a deal?

708
00:58:37,791 --> 00:58:41,041
Marfil, that's enough!
You don't know what you're talking about.

709
00:58:43,333 --> 00:58:45,916
The last time you sent me abroad was
when Mom died.

710
00:58:47,208 --> 00:58:48,333
And now again.

711
00:58:50,541 --> 00:58:52,166
What's going on, Dad?

712
00:58:53,041 --> 00:58:55,750
I just told you. We're moving.

713
00:58:56,833 --> 00:58:58,791
So, you'd better get used to the idea.

714
00:59:22,958 --> 00:59:25,541
PRIVATE PROPERTY
NO TRESPASSING

715
00:59:30,125 --> 00:59:31,250
Good boy.

716
00:59:48,458 --> 00:59:49,500
Mr. Cortés.

717
00:59:50,250 --> 00:59:51,625
Is everything set for tomorrow?

718
00:59:52,333 --> 00:59:54,208
We've tapped the cameras
at the racetrack.

719
00:59:55,000 --> 00:59:57,083
We'll finally know
what Marcus Kozel looks like.

720
00:59:57,583 --> 01:00:00,708
- We just need him to attend the meeting.
- He'll be there.

721
01:00:01,666 --> 01:00:04,999
I'm offering him my routes.
I'm putting an end to our war.

722
01:00:05,000 --> 01:00:08,374
If you hadn't avenged Natasha's death,
there'd be no war to put an end to.

723
01:00:08,375 --> 01:00:10,250
Natasha's murder, Logan.

724
01:00:11,291 --> 01:00:13,083
Marcus Kozel murdered my wife.

725
01:00:15,375 --> 01:00:16,583
And almost my daughter too.

726
01:00:17,583 --> 01:00:19,041
Marfil was with her?

727
01:00:20,125 --> 01:00:23,040
They cut the brakes on her car
and she crashed into a truck

728
01:00:23,041 --> 01:00:24,958
when she picked up Marfil
from ballet class.

729
01:00:26,041 --> 01:00:28,041
Natasha swerved and took the hit,

730
01:00:28,666 --> 01:00:30,415
and Marfil was unharmed.

731
01:00:30,416 --> 01:00:31,957
Until the kidnapping.

732
01:00:31,958 --> 01:00:33,583
I thought she'd be safe in New York.

733
01:00:35,041 --> 01:00:36,958
Far from the reach of that bastard.

734
01:00:40,583 --> 01:00:43,208
If I had finished him,
he wouldn't have kidnapped Marfil.

735
01:00:43,916 --> 01:00:46,125
And I wouldn't have had to ask
for your help.

736
01:00:47,583 --> 01:00:49,958
I want someone to stay
and keep an eye on my daughters.

737
01:00:50,708 --> 01:00:53,665
Marfil knows I'm hiding something,
and I don't want any surprises.

738
01:00:53,666 --> 01:00:55,666
I'll stay here with them.

739
01:00:56,750 --> 01:00:58,833
The Russians can't suspect a thing.

740
01:00:59,875 --> 01:01:02,083
You have no idea what they're capable of.

741
01:01:10,583 --> 01:01:11,625
My baby.

742
01:01:20,958 --> 01:01:23,832
I just wanted to ride Yaco.
I didn't stray far from the house.

743
01:01:23,833 --> 01:01:25,041
That's not why I'm here.

744
01:01:25,875 --> 01:01:29,500
- Your dad says you're moving to Argentina.
- You wanted distance. There you have it.

745
01:01:30,916 --> 01:01:33,624
When I said that,
I was trying to spare us a problem.

746
01:01:33,625 --> 01:01:35,540
For me, it's not a problem.

747
01:01:35,541 --> 01:01:36,875
Marfil, it's not possible.

748
01:01:37,625 --> 01:01:38,708
Can't you see that?

749
01:01:39,375 --> 01:01:41,458
- Our worlds are very different.
- So what?

750
01:01:42,291 --> 01:01:45,666
Okay, I understand you're upset,
but it's for the best.

751
01:01:46,208 --> 01:01:47,707
One day, you'll understand.

752
01:01:47,708 --> 01:01:48,708
Wow.

753
01:01:49,208 --> 01:01:51,040
That's such a grown-up phrase.

754
01:01:51,041 --> 01:01:54,415
I'd expect that from a brat in my college,
but I thought you were smarter.

755
01:01:54,416 --> 01:01:56,332
At least they'd be able to give you
what you want.

756
01:01:56,333 --> 01:01:57,999
You have no idea what I want.

757
01:01:58,000 --> 01:01:59,415
I know I can't give it to you.

758
01:01:59,416 --> 01:02:00,791
So what does all this mean?

759
01:02:01,791 --> 01:02:03,415
It was just a kiss. Come on.

760
01:02:03,416 --> 01:02:05,583
Really? And why did you kiss me?

761
01:02:07,625 --> 01:02:09,957
I don't know. I wasn't thinking.

762
01:02:09,958 --> 01:02:11,624
- You weren't thinking.
- No.

763
01:02:11,625 --> 01:02:12,625
You're lying.

764
01:02:14,250 --> 01:02:16,208
You let me hit you
so I could get that date.

765
01:02:19,250 --> 01:02:21,208
You're not fooling me.
Don't fool yourself.

766
01:02:54,750 --> 01:02:55,750
Marfil?

767
01:02:58,208 --> 01:02:59,916
Coming! Just a second!

768
01:03:05,416 --> 01:03:07,207
Your father awaits you for dinner.

769
01:03:07,208 --> 01:03:09,207
Sebastian was helping me bring Yaco in.

770
01:03:09,208 --> 01:03:10,500
So you are done, then.

771
01:03:11,208 --> 01:03:14,332
- No. We still have to tidy up and--
- Don't worry.

772
01:03:14,333 --> 01:03:15,708
I'll take care of it.

773
01:03:40,000 --> 01:03:42,374
- What will you say to Wilson?
- That you're sleeping

774
01:03:42,375 --> 01:03:44,415
- and you've felt bad since last night.
- Good.

775
01:03:44,416 --> 01:03:45,665
What if he finds out?

776
01:03:45,666 --> 01:03:46,874
Say that I lied to you.

777
01:03:46,875 --> 01:03:48,750
I don't want you to get into trouble.

778
01:03:49,291 --> 01:03:52,165
- Dad has forbidden us to leave the house.
- I don't care.

779
01:03:52,166 --> 01:03:54,333
I need to know what he's hiding from us.

780
01:04:09,000 --> 01:04:10,666
Should we go straight to the box?

781
01:05:24,208 --> 01:05:25,749
- Are you all right?
- It's nothing.

782
01:05:25,750 --> 01:05:27,332
- Yes. I'm fine.
- Are you sure?

783
01:05:27,333 --> 01:05:28,665
- Are you all right?
- Yes.

784
01:05:28,666 --> 01:05:31,707
My bad. I was distracted
watching the race. I'm sorry.

785
01:05:31,708 --> 01:05:33,999
In that case, good luck with the bets.

786
01:05:34,000 --> 01:05:36,707
I don't bet. I buy horses, actually.

787
01:05:36,708 --> 01:05:40,415
I've got my eye on a few.
I love Cortés' horses.

788
01:05:40,416 --> 01:05:42,500
You're going to buy my father's horses?

789
01:05:43,750 --> 01:05:46,083
- You are Alejandro Cortés' daughter?
- That's right.

790
01:05:46,916 --> 01:05:48,125
Unbelievable.

791
01:05:49,458 --> 01:05:52,124
Well, my name is Iván.

792
01:05:52,125 --> 01:05:54,457
- Marfil.
- It's a pleasure. That's a lovely name.

793
01:05:54,458 --> 01:05:56,875
- Thank you.
- We could discuss it.

794
01:05:57,541 --> 01:05:59,999
The horse thing. If you want.

795
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:02,041
We could have a drink and talk about it.

796
01:06:03,333 --> 01:06:06,415
- But if you're busy, I won't bother you.
- No.

797
01:06:06,416 --> 01:06:08,041
I wasn't doing anything. Shall we?

798
01:06:08,750 --> 01:06:09,875
All right. Let's go.

799
01:06:11,625 --> 01:06:13,791
- Do you ride?
- Not so much anymore.

800
01:06:16,541 --> 01:06:17,541
They're here.

801
01:06:39,250 --> 01:06:40,541
Cortés.

802
01:06:41,041 --> 01:06:43,083
Kozel. Finally.

803
01:06:43,666 --> 01:06:44,666
Yes.

804
01:06:45,833 --> 01:06:48,125
You made a very good decision.

805
01:06:49,291 --> 01:06:52,916
For you and your family.

806
01:06:54,333 --> 01:06:55,208
For everyone.

807
01:07:11,083 --> 01:07:12,208
Come on.

808
01:07:13,541 --> 01:07:16,749
There he is. Nice to meet you, Mr. Kozel.

809
01:07:16,750 --> 01:07:19,458
It's a shame you have to go.
I was having a great time.

810
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:21,625
I know. So was I.

811
01:07:22,500 --> 01:07:25,457
We could meet up some other time.

812
01:07:25,458 --> 01:07:27,540
Are you dating anyone?

813
01:07:27,541 --> 01:07:29,125
Are you always this straightforward?

814
01:07:29,750 --> 01:07:33,500
I think that when you want something,
you just have to go for it.

815
01:07:34,041 --> 01:07:35,708
An ambitious belief.

816
01:07:36,291 --> 01:07:38,250
You have to be ambitious
when it's worth it.

817
01:07:40,541 --> 01:07:43,416
No. I'm not dating anyone.

818
01:07:45,208 --> 01:07:48,041
Would you give me your phone number?

819
01:07:49,875 --> 01:07:52,291
The thing is I'm moving to Buenos Aires.

820
01:07:52,875 --> 01:07:53,916
Buenos Aires?

821
01:07:55,750 --> 01:07:58,915
That's the worst excuse I've ever heard.
I've heard some good ones.

822
01:07:58,916 --> 01:08:00,915
- That's the worst one.
- It's not an excuse.

823
01:08:00,916 --> 01:08:03,208
My father is selling the house,
now the horses...

824
01:08:04,833 --> 01:08:08,415
Well, I travel a lot.
I could come visit you.

825
01:08:08,416 --> 01:08:09,790
Of course.

826
01:08:09,791 --> 01:08:14,250
What if I told you
that I already want to see you again?

827
01:08:15,458 --> 01:08:17,000
I'm still here.

828
01:08:18,000 --> 01:08:19,750
And what if I told you

829
01:08:21,125 --> 01:08:23,750
that I've been thinking
about kissing you all this time?

830
01:08:27,750 --> 01:08:28,750
What would you say?

831
01:08:32,291 --> 01:08:33,707
Ray, you got him?

832
01:08:33,708 --> 01:08:35,041
<i>We got him, buddy.</i>

833
01:08:35,500 --> 01:08:36,458
Thanks, man.

834
01:08:43,958 --> 01:08:45,833
It was a pleasure, Marfil.

835
01:08:58,625 --> 01:09:00,874
- Marfil, where are you going?
- I need to be alone.

836
01:09:00,875 --> 01:09:02,040
I'm coming with you.

837
01:09:02,041 --> 01:09:04,624
No, Gabi, you're not coming.
I'd rather you stay here.

838
01:09:04,625 --> 01:09:07,415
What do you mean?
We were going to spend the day together.

839
01:09:07,416 --> 01:09:09,041
I've changed my mind.

840
01:09:10,708 --> 01:09:13,166
- What happened at the racecourse?
- I told you, nothing.

841
01:09:15,208 --> 01:09:17,125
Okay. Sebastian, Marfil is leaving!

842
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:21,166
Shit.

843
01:09:22,500 --> 01:09:23,583
Come on, come on.

844
01:09:25,791 --> 01:09:26,875
What are you doing?

845
01:09:45,375 --> 01:09:48,791
You can't just walk out
and ditch Wilson like that.

846
01:09:51,000 --> 01:09:52,749
What were you doing at the racecourse?

847
01:09:52,750 --> 01:09:54,041
It was just a kiss.

848
01:09:56,708 --> 01:09:57,999
That's not what I meant.

849
01:09:58,000 --> 01:10:00,624
You think I don't know
you're hiding things from me?

850
01:10:00,625 --> 01:10:02,790
Something's going on
and nobody will tell me.

851
01:10:02,791 --> 01:10:06,457
This is not a game.
You can't just go off on your own.

852
01:10:06,458 --> 01:10:09,999
I'll have to get used to it,
soon I won't have a babysitter anymore.

853
01:10:10,000 --> 01:10:11,540
Besides, what do you care?

854
01:10:11,541 --> 01:10:14,249
I care because
I don't want anything to happen to you.

855
01:10:14,250 --> 01:10:17,124
Are you saying that
as my bodyguard or as Sebastian?

856
01:10:17,125 --> 01:10:19,375
Both. Okay?

857
01:10:20,708 --> 01:10:22,291
Can you slow down, please?

858
01:10:28,166 --> 01:10:29,000
Shit.

859
01:10:30,250 --> 01:10:32,625
- What is it?
- The brakes aren't working.

860
01:10:39,291 --> 01:10:40,916
- What do I do?
- Focus on one point.

861
01:10:41,541 --> 01:10:44,416
- What do I do? Sebastian, what do I do?
- Straighten the wheel.

862
01:10:45,041 --> 01:10:47,583
Keep it that way.

863
01:10:50,458 --> 01:10:53,625
- Two cars coming at us. What do I do?
- On my mark, swerve to the left.

864
01:10:54,583 --> 01:10:55,665
Now!

865
01:10:55,666 --> 01:10:56,500
Shit!

866
01:11:06,916 --> 01:11:08,041
Stay clear!

867
01:11:10,833 --> 01:11:12,582
Watch out! Roadworks ahead!

868
01:11:12,583 --> 01:11:14,166
- What are you going to do?
- Trust me.

869
01:11:27,541 --> 01:11:29,790
<i>Wilson, we were in Alejandro's car.</i>

870
01:11:29,791 --> 01:11:31,665
They were trying to kill him.

871
01:11:31,666 --> 01:11:33,250
You need to leave now.

872
01:11:34,083 --> 01:11:35,541
<i>Yeah, I'm taking Gabriela away.</i>

873
01:11:45,041 --> 01:11:47,290
- Dad.
<i>- Tell me you're all right.</i>

874
01:11:47,291 --> 01:11:48,791
Yes, don't worry.

875
01:11:49,541 --> 01:11:51,791
It was just a little bump.
We're both fine.

876
01:11:53,791 --> 01:11:57,541
Go back to New York. I'll come get you
and we'll leave for Buenos Aires.

877
01:11:58,416 --> 01:11:59,875
<i>I need you to trust me.</i>

878
01:12:01,166 --> 01:12:03,000
<i>I know I owe you a lot of explanations.</i>

879
01:12:03,541 --> 01:12:05,166
<i>I promise I'll tell you everything.</i>

880
01:12:06,625 --> 01:12:07,833
<i>Marfil...</i>

881
01:12:08,958 --> 01:12:09,958
I love you, honey.

882
01:12:17,833 --> 01:12:23,999
NEW YORK

883
01:12:24,000 --> 01:12:26,915
<i>Wilson has brought me to London.
What's going on?</i>

884
01:12:26,916 --> 01:12:28,957
Gabi, I need to ask you a favor.

885
01:12:28,958 --> 01:12:29,791
<i>What?</i>

886
01:12:30,500 --> 01:12:32,458
Stay close to Wilson at all times.

887
01:12:33,291 --> 01:12:35,040
Do not leave the boarding school.

888
01:12:35,041 --> 01:12:37,916
<i>What if the boarding school's
security fails?</i>

889
01:12:38,666 --> 01:12:41,416
<i>- Or Wilson? Then what?</i>
- I'll come to protect you myself.

890
01:12:42,458 --> 01:12:44,125
I'll never let anything happen to you.

891
01:12:44,958 --> 01:12:46,041
Never.

892
01:12:46,958 --> 01:12:47,958
I promise.

893
01:13:10,083 --> 01:13:11,083
Are you okay?

894
01:13:11,875 --> 01:13:13,666
I'll feel better when I take this.

895
01:13:22,625 --> 01:13:24,250
I just wanted to say thank you.

896
01:13:26,041 --> 01:13:28,541
<i>When the accident happened,
you swerved to take the hit.</i>

897
01:13:29,666 --> 01:13:30,916
I did what I had to do.

898
01:13:31,375 --> 01:13:33,333
I don't want anything
to happen to you either.

899
01:13:34,125 --> 01:13:35,625
I've grown fond of you over time.

900
01:13:36,708 --> 01:13:38,041
Even if you don't like it.

901
01:14:00,333 --> 01:14:01,666
Why are you looking at me?

902
01:14:05,625 --> 01:14:06,875
What are you doing?

903
01:14:20,750 --> 01:14:21,750
No.

904
01:14:26,500 --> 01:14:28,125
For fuck's sake.

905
01:14:51,750 --> 01:14:52,750
I do like it.

906
01:14:54,791 --> 01:14:56,250
That you've grown fond of me.

907
01:15:01,333 --> 01:15:02,375
I like you.

908
01:15:06,083 --> 01:15:09,416
I thought you'd be unbearable.

909
01:15:11,625 --> 01:15:12,666
Wow.

910
01:15:13,833 --> 01:15:15,916
Confessing your feelings
isn't your strong suit.

911
01:15:16,666 --> 01:15:17,791
But you're not.

912
01:15:21,791 --> 01:15:22,708
You're beautiful.

913
01:15:25,333 --> 01:15:26,541
Smart.

914
01:15:29,166 --> 01:15:31,833
Brave. Determined and--

915
01:17:25,708 --> 01:17:27,166
We need to get ready.

916
01:17:28,458 --> 01:17:29,750
I don't want to go.

917
01:17:32,083 --> 01:17:33,250
You'll be all right there.

918
01:17:34,166 --> 01:17:36,041
It'll be like starting from scratch.

919
01:17:43,750 --> 01:17:45,458
Sebastian, I can wait for you.

920
01:17:47,625 --> 01:17:49,875
These past few months
I've been so happy with you.

921
01:17:52,750 --> 01:17:54,166
I'm going to miss you very much.

922
01:17:56,791 --> 01:17:58,541
Eventually you will forget everything.

923
01:18:04,041 --> 01:18:05,625
An elephant never forgets.

924
01:18:50,625 --> 01:18:51,625
Logan!

925
01:18:53,500 --> 01:18:54,750
We're leaving, Logan!

926
01:19:42,791 --> 01:19:43,625
Kozel.

927
01:19:44,666 --> 01:19:46,291
I am not Marcus Kozel.

928
01:19:47,375 --> 01:19:48,875
I think you're looking for me.

929
01:19:50,958 --> 01:19:52,791
Hello, Alejandro.

930
01:19:54,833 --> 01:19:57,625
You're probably more used
to doing business with my father.

931
01:20:00,416 --> 01:20:02,916
It's a pity you killed him
by blowing up his plane.

932
01:20:04,208 --> 01:20:05,833
But now I'm in charge.

933
01:20:07,208 --> 01:20:09,625
Rumor has it you tried to trick me.

934
01:20:10,291 --> 01:20:11,666
I don't like being lied to.

935
01:20:12,958 --> 01:20:16,000
I don't know what you've been told,
but it's not true.

936
01:20:19,791 --> 01:20:20,916
I met Marfil.

937
01:20:23,791 --> 01:20:27,166
You have a truly gorgeous daughter.

938
01:20:28,291 --> 01:20:29,375
She's beautiful.

939
01:20:39,166 --> 01:20:40,833
- Are you ready?
- Almost.

940
01:20:51,208 --> 01:20:52,208
What's that?

941
01:20:54,625 --> 01:20:55,750
It was my mother's.

942
01:20:56,875 --> 01:20:57,875
Look.

943
01:21:13,000 --> 01:21:14,041
Sebastian.

944
01:21:23,166 --> 01:21:25,583
No!

945
01:21:30,875 --> 01:21:33,290
- Are you okay? You're hit!
- It's nothing.

946
01:21:33,291 --> 01:21:35,082
- Breathe.
- Okay.

947
01:21:35,083 --> 01:21:38,333
- Go to the door. I'll cover you.
- No, I'm not leaving you alone.

948
01:21:40,708 --> 01:21:42,999
- Are you sure?
- Trust me. I'll be right behind you.

949
01:21:43,000 --> 01:21:44,000
Okay.

950
01:21:46,500 --> 01:21:47,833
- Okay.
- Okay.

951
01:22:17,041 --> 01:22:19,000
- They're coming that way.
- This way.

952
01:22:24,083 --> 01:22:25,375
This way, come on.

953
01:22:59,875 --> 01:23:04,625
What are you doing? Not her! Not her!
We were told that she should be alive.

954
01:23:05,708 --> 01:23:07,957
- Let me go first. They won't shoot me.
- No!

955
01:23:07,958 --> 01:23:08,791
Sebastian!

956
01:23:10,375 --> 01:23:11,707
Get behind me!

957
01:23:11,708 --> 01:23:13,291
No, no way. Are you crazy?

958
01:23:21,166 --> 01:23:23,166
Don't come any closer. I said,
Don't come any closer.

959
01:23:27,000 --> 01:23:28,625
Freeze! Freeze!

960
01:23:39,791 --> 01:23:41,500
- Watch it! Watch it!
- Go! Go!

961
01:23:49,458 --> 01:23:50,750
Stop! Don't move!

962
01:23:53,833 --> 01:23:55,458
Put her in the van!

963
01:23:56,333 --> 01:23:57,541
<i>Put her in the van!</i>

964
01:23:58,416 --> 01:23:59,833
<i>Put her in the van!</i>

965
01:24:00,875 --> 01:24:02,333
<i>Put her in the van!</i>

966
01:24:05,916 --> 01:24:06,916
Come on.

967
01:24:11,958 --> 01:24:13,916
Sebastian, are you okay? Your arm?

968
01:24:15,791 --> 01:24:17,625
It's not serious. Don't worry.

969
01:24:20,791 --> 01:24:22,083
What the fuck are you doing?

970
01:24:22,916 --> 01:24:25,041
- I remember you.
- Marfil.

971
01:24:25,833 --> 01:24:27,750
- "Put her in the van."
- Marfil.

972
01:24:28,416 --> 01:24:29,875
That's what you said.

973
01:24:31,666 --> 01:24:33,000
To you, specifically.

974
01:24:36,291 --> 01:24:38,208
You two kidnapped me.

975
01:24:43,416 --> 01:24:44,416
Who are you?

976
01:25:19,375 --> 01:25:21,500
What does the FBI
have to do with all this?

977
01:25:22,083 --> 01:25:23,291
Why did you kidnap me?

978
01:25:25,333 --> 01:25:27,416
- To frighten your dad.
- Why?

979
01:25:28,708 --> 01:25:30,208
We wanted him to ask for our help.

980
01:25:30,875 --> 01:25:32,458
He did and we made a deal.

981
01:25:33,583 --> 01:25:34,500
A deal?

982
01:25:36,333 --> 01:25:40,249
- Information in exchange for protection.
- To protect us from whom?

983
01:25:40,250 --> 01:25:44,166
Your dad's involved in dangerous business.
And he has even worse enemies.

984
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:47,665
You make him sound like a criminal,
but he's not.

985
01:25:47,666 --> 01:25:51,249
My dad is an honest, hardworking man
who has earned everything he has.

986
01:25:51,250 --> 01:25:54,000
- And you don't know what the fuck you're--
- Your dad did this.

987
01:25:54,916 --> 01:25:57,790
He tried to kill one of his associates,
Marcus Kozel.

988
01:25:57,791 --> 01:26:01,540
He blew up his plane
and still failed to kill him.

989
01:26:01,541 --> 01:26:02,666
But 20 of his men died.

990
01:26:06,333 --> 01:26:08,707
There were going to be consequences,
sooner or later.

991
01:26:08,708 --> 01:26:11,082
All right, we kidnapped you.

992
01:26:11,083 --> 01:26:13,875
But if we hadn't, something much worse
could've happened to you.

993
01:26:33,125 --> 01:26:34,166
Don't, Sebastian.

994
01:26:35,916 --> 01:26:37,291
It's okay. Let her process it.

995
01:26:48,833 --> 01:26:50,250
Where the fuck is Cortés?

996
01:26:51,708 --> 01:26:52,957
She has to leave now!

997
01:26:52,958 --> 01:26:55,499
He'll let us know
when he arrives in New York.

998
01:26:55,500 --> 01:26:57,833
He better hurry up,
because, otherwise, we're fucked.

999
01:27:07,916 --> 01:27:10,999
My dad. He's coming to pick me up.
He sent me a location.

1000
01:27:11,000 --> 01:27:13,208
- Where?
- Times Square.

1001
01:27:13,833 --> 01:27:15,541
- He wants me to go alone.
- No.

1002
01:27:17,166 --> 01:27:19,082
- I don't like it.
- Buddy, think.

1003
01:27:19,083 --> 01:27:21,999
If they don't get on that plane
and leave for Buenos Aires,

1004
01:27:22,000 --> 01:27:24,040
it could be worse
than what happened tonight.

1005
01:27:24,041 --> 01:27:27,250
I don't care what you say, I'm going.
I need to see him.

1006
01:27:30,875 --> 01:27:31,958
Okay.

1007
01:27:32,541 --> 01:27:34,124
But I'll be following you closely.

1008
01:27:34,125 --> 01:27:36,374
And if anything happens, no matter what,

1009
01:27:36,375 --> 01:27:39,000
I'm getting you out of there. Understood?

1010
01:27:42,125 --> 01:27:46,708
The most important thing is
that you keep your phone close to you.

1011
01:27:47,291 --> 01:27:49,291
It's the only way for us to locate you.

1012
01:27:51,541 --> 01:27:52,541
It's ready.

1013
01:27:59,458 --> 01:28:00,958
It doesn't look like a mic.

1014
01:28:02,166 --> 01:28:03,166
That's the idea.

1015
01:28:04,541 --> 01:28:06,749
I need a code word.

1016
01:28:06,750 --> 01:28:09,249
Something that will let me know
you're in danger.

1017
01:28:09,250 --> 01:28:10,083
"Ebony"?

1018
01:28:11,916 --> 01:28:14,916
"Ebony And Ivory." The song
by Stevie Wonder and Paul McCartney.

1019
01:28:15,875 --> 01:28:18,041
What do you guys listen to? Reggaeton?

1020
01:28:18,875 --> 01:28:20,416
For lack of a better one, "ebony."

1021
01:28:21,208 --> 01:28:22,208
Okay.

1022
01:28:42,000 --> 01:28:45,375
I'll go look for something
I left somewhere around here.

1023
01:28:52,541 --> 01:28:53,541
Forgive me.

1024
01:28:57,916 --> 01:29:00,125
I couldn't tell you I was an FBI agent.

1025
01:29:03,000 --> 01:29:04,000
Marfil,

1026
01:29:04,875 --> 01:29:07,832
what we've had
is the only thing that is real

1027
01:29:07,833 --> 01:29:10,458
and the only thing
that has made this job worthwhile.

1028
01:29:11,375 --> 01:29:14,625
You're telling me this because
we're not going to see each other again.

1029
01:29:17,583 --> 01:29:19,666
We're going into witness protection.

1030
01:29:20,750 --> 01:29:22,666
That's why we have to leave the country.

1031
01:29:33,750 --> 01:29:35,790
If I never see you again,
I want you to know--

1032
01:29:35,791 --> 01:29:37,791
No, please. Don't say it.

1033
01:29:38,833 --> 01:29:40,375
It's the only thing I want to hear.

1034
01:29:40,958 --> 01:29:43,833
If you tell me that, I won't let you go.

1035
01:29:48,916 --> 01:29:50,041
Goodbye, Sebastian.

1036
01:29:53,291 --> 01:29:54,583
Goodbye, Elephant.

1037
01:30:25,041 --> 01:30:27,333
Okay. I'm in position.

1038
01:30:30,041 --> 01:30:31,208
Ray.

1039
01:30:32,208 --> 01:30:33,625
I got her, buddy.

1040
01:30:55,166 --> 01:30:56,665
Ray, talk to me.

1041
01:30:56,666 --> 01:30:57,708
Give me a sec, hold on.

1042
01:30:58,791 --> 01:31:00,375
Heads up, we've got movement.

1043
01:31:01,458 --> 01:31:03,375
- Who is it? Alejandro?
- <i>No.</i>

1044
01:31:04,000 --> 01:31:05,041
Marfil!

1045
01:31:06,500 --> 01:31:07,624
Logan?

1046
01:31:07,625 --> 01:31:09,332
I'm so happy to see you.

1047
01:31:09,333 --> 01:31:10,749
<i>Thank goodness you're okay.</i>

1048
01:31:10,750 --> 01:31:12,916
Logan? What the hell is he doing here?

1049
01:31:13,750 --> 01:31:14,833
I'm going to get her.

1050
01:31:16,041 --> 01:31:18,416
Wait, Sebastian.
Give it a minute. See what happens.

1051
01:31:22,041 --> 01:31:23,083
Where's my father?

1052
01:31:24,500 --> 01:31:27,625
- I'll take you to him now. Shall we?
- Okay.

1053
01:31:41,375 --> 01:31:43,791
<i>Go, they're between 44th and 7th.</i>

1054
01:31:45,416 --> 01:31:46,416
I see them.

1055
01:32:24,750 --> 01:32:26,041
<i>I lost them, Ray.</i>

1056
01:32:27,750 --> 01:32:29,790
<i>Ray, where are they?
Where the fuck are they?</i>

1057
01:32:29,791 --> 01:32:31,458
Stop, it's not that easy.

1058
01:32:32,291 --> 01:32:34,083
Where the fuck are they now?

1059
01:32:40,000 --> 01:32:41,250
Fucking hell.

1060
01:32:48,166 --> 01:32:49,290
There they are. I've got them.

1061
01:32:49,291 --> 01:32:51,665
I'm sending you the location
of Marfil's phone.

1062
01:32:51,666 --> 01:32:53,582
There it is.
They're walking into a parking lot

1063
01:32:53,583 --> 01:32:55,790
<i>between 43rd and 6th.</i>

1064
01:32:55,791 --> 01:32:57,082
Why didn't Dad come get me?

1065
01:32:57,083 --> 01:32:59,249
It wouldn't be safe
for Alejandro to be here.

1066
01:32:59,250 --> 01:33:00,875
I'll explain everything on the way.

1067
01:33:02,208 --> 01:33:03,124
Come on.

1068
01:33:03,125 --> 01:33:04,958
<i>You're 100 meters away. Hurry.</i>

1069
01:33:09,791 --> 01:33:11,666
I'm tapping into the parking lot cameras.

1070
01:33:12,916 --> 01:33:14,958
- Is my dad in there?
- No.

1071
01:33:15,750 --> 01:33:18,124
- You were going to take me to him.
- I am. Let's go.

1072
01:33:18,125 --> 01:33:20,750
I'm not taking one more step
until you tell me where he is.

1073
01:33:21,958 --> 01:33:23,625
I see it. I'm 10 meters away.

1074
01:33:24,375 --> 01:33:26,541
<i>Ray, what floor are they on?</i>

1075
01:33:27,750 --> 01:33:30,583
- <i>Ray.</i>
- The cameras aren't working. Fuck me.

1076
01:33:31,500 --> 01:33:32,708
He had to run away.

1077
01:33:34,458 --> 01:33:35,625
What? Why?

1078
01:33:37,416 --> 01:33:40,833
Alejandro's businesses
aren't as legal as one might expect.

1079
01:33:42,000 --> 01:33:45,291
He had a deal with the FBI,
but they have betrayed us.

1080
01:33:46,083 --> 01:33:48,499
Motherfucker. What is he talking about?

1081
01:33:48,500 --> 01:33:50,833
<i>I don't like this one bit. Hurry!</i>

1082
01:34:03,666 --> 01:34:07,708
If we don't leave here right now,
you may never see him again.

1083
01:34:09,333 --> 01:34:11,332
You are in danger too, Marfil.

1084
01:34:11,333 --> 01:34:13,999
And there is only one person
who can help us.

1085
01:34:14,000 --> 01:34:15,916
Ray, I can't hear you.

1086
01:34:27,166 --> 01:34:28,250
<i>Buddy!</i>

1087
01:35:14,250 --> 01:35:15,250
Hello, Marfil.

1088
01:35:17,041 --> 01:35:18,208
Iván?

1089
01:35:19,166 --> 01:35:20,624
Who the hell is Iván?

1090
01:35:20,625 --> 01:35:23,666
He's the one who's going to help us.
Get in, please.

1091
01:35:27,125 --> 01:35:29,000
<i>Ray, it's a trap.</i>

1092
01:35:31,083 --> 01:35:33,000
What is this?
Do you know where my father is?

1093
01:35:34,208 --> 01:35:35,333
All in due time.

1094
01:35:44,916 --> 01:35:46,208
Logan, what is going on?

1095
01:35:47,666 --> 01:35:48,708
Logan!

1096
01:35:59,750 --> 01:36:01,708
Marfil, may I?

1097
01:36:12,458 --> 01:36:13,750
Let's go.

1098
01:36:17,625 --> 01:36:18,750
Got anything to say?

1099
01:36:19,416 --> 01:36:20,458
Ebony.

1100
01:36:44,791 --> 01:36:51,791
THE STORY CONTINUES IN
DRAWN APART